{
  "_readme": "TEMPLATE ONLY. Copy this file to registry.json (same folder) and edit it. Nothing listed here is loaded or downloaded until the weights file actually exists on disk AND the entry is in registry.json. BlueEye never fabricates weights - a model shows 'not installed' until you place its .pt file (or provide a download_url). Full documentation: models/custom/README.md. Optional fields: auto (default true; set false to keep a model out of 'auto'), habitat, architecture, readiness ('needs_training' | 'incompatible'), status_note, limitations, metrics (object of label->value), video_verified (set true only after a real video test), type ('yolov8' | 'rtdetr'), and - for a real download - download_url plus sha256. Models that cannot run today are kept in models/custom/inactive_models.json instead.",
